WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:04.224
Game, Film, Food, htclig.

00:00:04.224 --> 00:00:07.520
Long ago, The four channels lived together
in harmony.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:11.080
But then everything changed when the YouTube
algorithm attacked.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:15.299
Only Matpat, master of all four theories,
could bring balance to the channels.

00:00:15.299 --> 00:00:17.630
But when YouTube needed him most, he vanished.

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:22.138
But I believe that Matpat can save the world.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.220
Hello Internet!

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:35.190
Welcome to Film Theory, the show that's here
to reveal your secret power: subscription bending.

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:35.832
Try it out.

00:00:35.832 --> 00:00:38.030
Click the button below the video to transform
it.

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:40.750
Now, I don't often call a lot of things perfect.

00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:43.200
Almost anything can be improved upon in one
way or another.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.080
But up there with Chrono Trigger, the Lord
of the Rings, and the sweet, delicious burn

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:50.000
of Diet Coke, is Avatar: The Last Airbender.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.510
If ever there was a perfect animated series,
it might just be Avatar.

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:54.699
In case you need a bit of a refresher.

00:00:54.699 --> 00:00:58.719
In the world of Avatar, people live in one
of four nations, each built around one of

00:00:58.719 --> 00:00:59.960
the four traditional elements.

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:03.840
You have the water tribes at the North and
South Poles, the vast earth kingdom that covers

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:08.540
most of the world's landmass, the industrious
and aggressive fire nation, and the elusive

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:10.610
flighty air nomad monks.

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:15.130
Some people are born with the ability to bend
one of these four elements, but only one person

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:17.430
can master all four of them.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:21.579
That one person is known as the Avatar and
is tasked with keeping the world in balance

00:01:21.579 --> 00:01:24.000
as the very first avatar Wan explains:

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:33.570
Each avatar is born into a cycle, water to
earth to fire to air, so that when the previous

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:36.810
avatar dies, a new one is born in the next
nation.

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:40.909
And over the course of the various seasons,
we watch as this exact cycle plays out.

00:01:40.909 --> 00:01:44.700
Avatar Kyoshi from the Earth Kingdom gives
way to Roku from the Fire Nation, who then

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:49.898
dies and opens the door to Aang from the Air
Nomads and finally Avatar Korra from the Water Tribe.

00:01:49.898 --> 00:01:54.150
It's a great set up that allows for stories
and characters outside of the original series

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:56.600
to be explored, expanding the world even further.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:00.100
I mean, that's basically what happened with
the sequel series, The Legend of Korra, and

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:03.320
it appears to be Nickelodeon's strategy with
the franchise moving forward.

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:08.285
There have been multiple novels and comic
books dedicated to other avatars and supporting characters.

00:02:08.285 --> 00:02:13.120
They've even established an entire production
studio devoted to more Avatar content.

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:16.489
Rumor has it that a bunch of this new stuff
is going to focus on different avatars too.

00:02:16.489 --> 00:02:20.860
Sure you have the OGs Aang and Korra as well
as the fan favorite Kyoshi, but also the next

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:22.980
avatar that we haven't even met yet.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:25.780
There's even a live action Netflix series
on the way.

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:27.461
Here's hoping it goes better than the last
one.

00:02:31.208 --> 00:02:35.920
Anyway, in my excitement for new Avatar content,
I decided to go rewatch the series and catch

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.770
up on a bunch of the spinoff stories that
they've released over the years.

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:39.770
And you know what, theorists?

00:02:39.770 --> 00:02:45.659
The more and more I look, the more and more
I realize that having an avatar sucks.

00:02:45.659 --> 00:02:49.860
This world is so much worse because of the
avatar cycle.

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:53.630
When you really break down what each avatar
does during their life and how it compares

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:55.890
to what each avatar is supposed to be doing.

00:02:55.890 --> 00:03:00.760
You realize that each and every one of them
has largely failed, enough so that you kind

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:04.550
of got to ask, is it even worth having an
avatar at all?

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:08.480
Hop aboard your flying bison and pour out
some cactus juice, loyal theorist.

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:12.319
I'm about to bend your ear over this broken,
ancient tradition.

00:03:12.319 --> 00:03:14.640
Let's start by setting our ground rules, shall
we?

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:17.890
Remember, the whole thing about the Avatar
is that their main goal is to keep the world

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:21.070
in balance, both physically and spiritually.

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:23.080
What exactly that means could be up for debate.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:28.210
But the way I see it, an Avatar's duties largely
break down into four main tasks: 1) helping

00:03:28.210 --> 00:03:30.580
keep international peace between the four
nations

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:34.680
2) helping keep internal peace within each
of those nations.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:37.659
3) Protecting innocent people and bringing
justice to the unjust.

00:03:37.659 --> 00:03:41.189
And 4) bridging the gap between the human
world and the spirit world.

00:03:41.189 --> 00:03:43.070
So let's just start at the beginning of our
list.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:46.610
One of the main parts of an avatar's duty
is to help keep international peace between

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:47.610
the four nations.

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:49.620
And admittedly, some of them are good at it.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:52.840
For instance, we see that Ang has helped to
set up an international government to help

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:54.750
the four nations stay at peace with each other.

00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:58.819
But literally, from the opening seconds of
the show, we know that at least one avatar

00:03:58.819 --> 00:04:01.269
had a major oopsie in this field.

00:04:06.881 --> 00:04:09.460
The 
whole premise of the entire franchise starts

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:13.730
with a giant international war, and it all
happened because of the failure of the avatars.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:18.061
On one hand, we could blame Aang who ran away
from his duties, which in turn opened up a

00:04:18.061 --> 00:04:20.919
power vacuum that allowed the 100 year war
to begin.

00:04:20.919 --> 00:04:25.419
But he was also literally 12 years old at
the time, so it’s kind of hard to fault

00:04:25.419 --> 00:04:26.419
him for that one.

00:04:26.419 --> 00:04:30.520
Instead, the true failure falls to Aang's
predecessor, Avatar Roku.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:34.480
Roku was childhood friends with Fire Lord
Sozin, the Fire Lord who started the war.

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:38.167
And what's worse, Roku knew that Sozin wanted
to conquer these other nations.

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:49.090
So what did Roku do to stop it?

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:54.119
He basically gave Sozin a slap on the wrist
and a stern talking to, by his own admission,

00:04:54.119 --> 00:04:58.259
Roku's indecisiveness, and let's be honest,
favoritism to his friend and home nation,

00:04:58.259 --> 00:05:02.739
was a huge weakness which ultimately led to
tons of unnecessary death.

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:22.639
Instead, his actions led to Sozin's betrayal,
his own death, and a war that lasted generations.

00:05:22.639 --> 00:05:26.669
His failure led to the complete annihilation
of the Air Nation, as well as all the loss

00:05:26.669 --> 00:05:28.669
of life that comes with a war of conquest.

00:05:28.669 --> 00:05:32.770
It’s not exactly going to be making WatchMojo's
top ten list of moments that brought balance

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:33.657
to the world.

00:05:33.657 --> 00:05:34.657
And here's the thing.

00:05:34.657 --> 00:05:38.009
We don't have to look at Roku or Aang to see
the avatar's failures here.

00:05:38.009 --> 00:05:42.770
In the prequel novels, we learned that Avatar
Szeto the Fire Nation Avatar before Roku was

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:45.680
born into a time of great strife for the nation.

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:49.590
And instead of working internationally, like
most other avatars, Szeto decided to focus

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:53.880
on the domestic politics, becoming a bureaucrat
within the fire nation to help his people.

00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:56.750
Though he helped shepherd the Fire Nation
back to prosperity.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:06:00.220
He did this at the expense of all the other
nations.

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:04.251
This eventually led to an event known as the
Platinum Affair shortly after his death, which

00:06:04.251 --> 00:06:09.176
saw the fire nation and water tribes secretly
backing a challenger to the Earth Kingdom throne.

00:06:09.176 --> 00:06:14.200
When this was discovered it led to all three
nations becoming incredibly isolationist.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:18.130
Because of this, Szeto’s immediate successor,
the air nomad Avatar Yangchen, would look

00:06:18.130 --> 00:06:20.520
back on Szeto's legacy as messy.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:24.830
So as you can already start to see, having
one person solely responsible for policing

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:28.560
the entire bending world is like an impossible
task.

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:32.050
Time is going to be the avatar’s most limited
resource and the decisions that they make

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:36.210
on how to spend that time inevitably means
that they're going to have to sacrifice one

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:37.789
major part of their duty.

00:06:37.789 --> 00:06:41.551
Obviously, for Szeto, focusing all of his
attention on bringing prosperity to the fire

00:06:41.551 --> 00:06:46.080
nation meant that he let conflicts arise within
other kingdoms with the Platinum Affair.

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:49.520
We see a similar situation arise in the Avatar
Kyoshi books.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:53.837
The Avatar before her, had a singular focus
on dealing with the spiritual duties of the role.

00:06:53.837 --> 00:06:56.930
This meant that he neglected his responsibilities
as a politician.

00:06:56.930 --> 00:07:00.789
His neglect of the physical world allowed
the Earth kingdom to become destabilized by

00:07:00.789 --> 00:07:05.752
infighting and Kyoshi was basically forced
to spend her entire life cleaning up that mess.

00:07:05.752 --> 00:07:07.300
But don't feel too bad for her.

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:09.610
She caused even more problems than she solved.

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:11.210
Case in point, Chin the Conqueror.

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:14.590
Now, this guy was a warlord standing up against
a corrupted king.

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:18.264
That said, Chin was far from a hero, as Kyoshi
herself says.

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:27.030
This seems like the exact sort of situation
where an avatar should stand up and help make

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:28.030
peace. Right?

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:32.169
A rebellion is threatening to destabilize
an entire kingdom and both sides are led by

00:07:32.169 --> 00:07:33.169
awful people.

00:07:33.169 --> 00:07:37.009
The keeper of peace and balance should probably
be looking into solving this issue.

00:07:37.009 --> 00:07:38.560
Even Kyoshi herself says.

00:07:41.949 --> 00:07:43.540
There's that word balance.

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:46.170
So what did Kyoshi do to stop Chin?

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:46.756
Nothing.

00:07:46.756 --> 00:07:47.454
Literally nothing.

00:07:47.454 --> 00:07:50.699
Chin was able to conquer almost the entire
continent.

00:07:50.699 --> 00:07:55.060
Kyoshi only decided to step in when he showed
up at her doorstep to take over the peninsula

00:07:55.060 --> 00:07:56.212
that she called home.

00:07:59.922 --> 00:08:00.980
Yeah, sure, Kyoshi.

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:02.949
Looks like you were getting right to that.

00:08:02.949 --> 00:08:06.710
So now that Chin is literally right in front
of her, you would think that this is a good

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:10.226
opportunity to try and stop his conquest and
restore balance to the Earth Kingdom.

00:08:10.226 --> 00:08:11.226
Nope!

00:08:11.226 --> 00:08:15.355
Kyoshi uses her power to disconnect the peninsula
from the mainland and then proceeds to yeet

00:08:15.355 --> 00:08:17.252
it out into the middle of the ocean.

00:08:17.252 --> 00:08:21.480
Seriously, in what's arguably the most impressive
display for an avatar is powers that we see

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:23.100
throughout the entire franchise.

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:26.020
All Kyoshi does is pull a giant: “ight,
Imma head out”.

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:29.430
Chin's conquest was only stopped because he
was too stubborn to get out of Kyoshi his

00:08:29.430 --> 00:08:32.608
way, falling to his death as Kyoshi Island
was being formed.

00:08:36.864 --> 00:08:38.090
Really Kyoshi?

00:08:38.090 --> 00:08:41.149
Sure looks like you got some massive revisionist
history going on there because you didn't

00:08:41.149 --> 00:08:43.959
do a gosh darn thing in the months leading
up to him coming to your peninsula.

00:08:43.959 --> 00:08:47.640
And that philosophy runs deep in the village
that Kyoshi leaves behind.

00:08:47.640 --> 00:08:51.209
Towards the beginning of the Last Airbender,
Team Avatar lands on Kyoshi Island, where

00:08:51.209 --> 00:08:53.650
the guiding wisdom of all the Kyoshi stans
is.

00:08:53.650 --> 00:08:55.247
“Yeah, it's not my problem”.

00:08:59.635 --> 00:09:04.220
Heck, even the Earth Kingdom Capitals catchphrase
“There is no war in Ba Sing Se”, follows

00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:05.310
the same attitude.

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:06.000
Ignore the problem.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:06.971
Deny.

00:09:06.971 --> 00:09:09.130
Close your eyes and it just goes away.

00:09:09.130 --> 00:09:12.550
Admittedly, things seem to go much better
under Roku's tenure. And after Aang ends the

00:09:12.550 --> 00:09:15.160
hundred year war, things again seem to go
smoothly.

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:18.500
But under Korra their civil conflict after
civil conflict.

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:20.860
She was Avatar during the water tribe civil
war.

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:24.910
Under her watch, the Red Lotus assassinates
the Earth Queen and in the aftermath Korra's

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:30.445
inaction due to injury and PTSD lets Kuvira
seize control of a great deal of the Earth Kingdom.

00:09:30.445 --> 00:09:33.440
Not a great track record in a long sequence
of avatars dropping the ball.

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:37.290
So now let's move on to our next criteria
protecting the innocent and bringing justice

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:38.290
to the unjust.

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:41.209
This one's a bit harder to judge because we
don't see a lot of the day to day lives of

00:09:41.209 --> 00:09:42.209
each avatar.

00:09:42.209 --> 00:09:45.900
And while yeah, we do see some heroic moments
like Aang Fighting Yakone and Korra chasing

00:09:45.900 --> 00:09:48.279
down bender criminals in the streets of Republic
City.

00:09:48.279 --> 00:09:52.820
There's a rotten core here that starts to
peek through the deeper we get into the franchise.

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:57.020
Most of The Legend of Korra’s plot revolves
around the idea of justice and what it takes

00:09:57.020 --> 00:09:58.310
to defend everyone.

00:09:58.310 --> 00:10:02.620
Korra’s first major adversary Amon is the
leader of a group called the Equalists, who

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:06.970
are all about leveling the playing field between
benders and non benders by taking away the

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:08.080
ability to bend.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:08.854
Sound insane?

00:10:08.854 --> 00:10:09.354
It is.

00:10:09.354 --> 00:10:13.250
But the movement is shown to resonate with
a lot of Republic City's citizens.

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:18.220
Life in the world of Avatar can be incredibly
hard for non benders, even in the new supposedly

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:20.490
harmonious society that Aang created.

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:22.930
If you're a bender, you have easy access to
jobs.

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:24.876
Power plants use fire benders to operate.

00:10:24.876 --> 00:10:29.650
Trains are powered by earth benders and policemen
are almost exclusively metal benders.

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:33.160
Benders also have a much easier time committing
acts of violence, as we're frequently shown

00:10:33.160 --> 00:10:36.510
groups of violent benders like the triple
threat triad, the Red Lotus.

00:10:36.510 --> 00:10:40.810
Heck, even the Republic City Police who treat
the use of force like it's second nature.

00:10:40.810 --> 00:10:41.910
Non benders are overlooked.

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:42.910
They're ignored.

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:44.490
They're frequently threatened.

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:48.690
In one particular scene, Republic City's metal
bending police force herd a group of non benders

00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:52.690
like cattle using force to break up a nonviolent
protest.

00:10:52.690 --> 00:10:56.089
These people are targeted because the police
force has turned off the power to their homes

00:10:56.089 --> 00:11:00.230
and they're peacefully resisting being profiled
as members of Amon's uprising just because

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:01.230
they aren't benders.

00:11:01.230 --> 00:11:04.871
A woman in the crowd makes a desperate plea
for Korra’s help, saying:

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:08.740
And Korra does help.

00:11:08.740 --> 00:11:09.307
Kinda.

00:11:09.307 --> 00:11:13.329
Unfortunately for the common people, Korra
considers the issue resolved after she outs

00:11:13.329 --> 00:11:18.070
Amon as a bender and a fraud, effectively
derailing a movement that began and grew thanks

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:22.459
to a genuine concern from a huge portion of
Republic City's non bending population.

00:11:22.459 --> 00:11:24.339
So that one doesn't look all that great for
Korra.

00:11:24.339 --> 00:11:26.959
But when you think about it, this is Aang’s
city.

00:11:26.959 --> 00:11:28.950
He created the system that Korra inherited.

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:32.790
In fact, this goes well beyond just Korra
and Aang.

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:37.060
The imbalance between benders and non benders
is a failure of every avatar before them who

00:11:37.060 --> 00:11:39.330
popped up or exploited the same system.

00:11:39.330 --> 00:11:43.209
Which brings us back to Kyoshi, who honestly
might have been the worst of the bunch.

00:11:43.209 --> 00:11:45.079
See,Kyoshi had herself a rough childhood.

00:11:45.079 --> 00:11:48.899
She was an orphan, working as a servant until
it was discovered that she was the avatar.

00:11:48.899 --> 00:11:51.529
She later joined a criminal gang that was
founded by her parents.

00:11:51.529 --> 00:11:55.579
And it's not like they suddenly stopped doing
crimes after the Avatar joined.

00:11:55.579 --> 00:11:56.184
Nope.

00:11:56.184 --> 00:11:57.850
They decided to involve Kyoshi in the crimes.

00:11:57.850 --> 00:12:01.920
And that's not all, Kyoshi youthful anger
heavily informed her way of thinking.

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:05.920
Even after learning that she was the avatar,
her thoughts were more centered on revenge

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:06.920
than duty.

00:12:06.920 --> 00:12:10.800
The Rise of Kyoshi states that quote: “Her
hunger to learn all four elements had nothing

00:12:10.800 --> 00:12:13.350
to do with becoming a fully realized avatar.

00:12:13.350 --> 00:12:17.959
Fire, air and water were simply more weapons
she could bring to bear on a single target.”

00:12:17.959 --> 00:12:18.959
end quote.

00:12:18.959 --> 00:12:22.850
And much later in her life, she was so unbothered
by taking a life that she didn't see a difference

00:12:22.850 --> 00:12:24.624
between accidents and intentional killings.

00:12:32.100 --> 00:12:33.339
As for protecting the innocent.

00:12:33.339 --> 00:12:34.959
Here again, we have some problems.

00:12:34.959 --> 00:12:39.149
In Shadow of Kyoshi, Kyoshi threatens to crush
a mother and her adult son to death with a

00:12:39.149 --> 00:12:43.980
boulder while trying to squeeze a false confession
out of them for something they didn't do.

00:12:43.980 --> 00:12:47.910
But her single worst decision is revealed
in the canonical flash game Escape From the

00:12:47.910 --> 00:12:48.930
Spirit World.

00:12:48.930 --> 00:12:51.370
It's here that Kyoshi confesses to Aang her
biggest failure.

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:55.220
See, one of the Earth Kings during Kyoshi's
life was incredibly unpopular.

00:12:55.220 --> 00:12:58.970
His leadership was seen as ineffective and
corrupt, and it eventually led to a peasant

00:12:58.970 --> 00:13:00.310
uprising against him.

00:13:00.310 --> 00:13:04.620
During the riots, the King ordered Kyoshi
to put the uprising down, and to her credit,

00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:05.620
she refused.

00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:09.480
Instead, she encouraged the king to listen
to the grievances of the people and find compromise.

00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:11.170
Seems pretty good so far, right?

00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:15.480
But here's the thing, Kyoshi admits that she
didn't like the people standing up against

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:16.480
the kingdom.

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:19.080
In fact, throughout the whole story, Kyoshi
seems less concerned about the human rights

00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:23.250
abuses committed by the king and more concerned
that the peasants are destroying historical

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:25.860
artifacts and upsetting the stability of the
monarchy.

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:29.610
So in exchange for the king listening to his
people and ending the riots, Kyoshi agrees

00:13:29.610 --> 00:13:32.300
to train an elite group of earth benders for
him.

00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:35.640
They would be, quote, “silent, precise and
feared by all”.

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:38.500
It was a force that would eventually be known
as the Dai Li.

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:39.000
Yup.

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:41.670
You remember those creepy secret police from
the animated series?

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:45.460
the ones with the rock gloves whose loyalty
could be bought and sold, and who sided with

00:13:45.460 --> 00:13:48.300
Azula and the fire nation during the invasion
of Ba Sing Se?

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:50.120
They were Kyoshi's idea.

00:13:50.120 --> 00:13:54.339
She even admits that she regrets not foreseeing
the long term consequences of giving future

00:13:54.339 --> 00:13:57.480
Earth Kingdom monarchs access to an elite
secret police force.

00:13:57.480 --> 00:14:00.920
But here's the thing, that move didn't make
sense even in her time period.

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:03.290
This king, the one that was ready to crush
his own people,

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:05.949
he shouldn't have had access to that secret
police force either.

00:14:05.949 --> 00:14:09.139
Imagine what he would have had them do to
the peasants if they were around to begin with.

00:14:09.139 --> 00:14:12.550
Then again, when you're as powerful as Kyoshi
and you treat your powers like a big ol’

00:14:12.550 --> 00:14:14.920
hammer, I guess everything looks like a nail.

00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:19.339
So again, for a lot of the avatars, protecting
the innocent and bringing justice to the unjust

00:14:19.339 --> 00:14:20.519
is just a bust.

00:14:20.519 --> 00:14:23.240
So that's three for three where a ton of avatars
fail.

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:25.490
But what about our fourth criteria here?

00:14:25.490 --> 00:14:28.070
Bridging the gap and keeping the peace between
the human and spirit worlds.

00:14:28.070 --> 00:14:31.480
This is basically THE thing that avatars are
supposed to be good at.

00:14:31.480 --> 00:14:33.959
Surely there isn't a legacy of failure here,
too.

00:14:33.959 --> 00:14:36.010
Well, you would think, and then you would
be wrong.

00:14:36.010 --> 00:14:39.889
We hear in the prequel novel dedicated to
Avatar Yangchen, that when humans and spirits

00:14:39.889 --> 00:14:43.330
came into conflict, she would strike bargains
that would get the spirits to leave humans

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:45.580
alone so long as they took care of the physical
world.

00:14:45.580 --> 00:14:49.050
And of course, humans did not live up to their
end of the deal.

00:14:49.050 --> 00:14:53.882
As a result, spirits wound up committing a
lot of violence against humans who broke their oaths.

00:14:53.882 --> 00:14:57.490
This, in turn, created a huge mess for the
next avatar, Kuruk, to clean up.

00:14:57.490 --> 00:15:01.291
We discover in the Kyoshi novels that Avatar
Kuruk would end up spending most of his short

00:15:01.291 --> 00:15:04.709
life fighting the dark spirits empowered by
Yangchen’s decisions.

00:15:04.709 --> 00:15:08.500
Finally, let's skip forward to Avatar Korra,
who might just have been the avatar to fail

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:09.980
the most at this one.

00:15:09.980 --> 00:15:14.100
At the end of the Legend of Korra Season two,
Korra’s subdued by her uncle Unalaq, who’s

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:16.070
merged with the Dark Spirit Vaatu.

00:15:16.070 --> 00:15:20.790
Unalaq is able to rip the Avatar spirit Raava
from Korra's body, severing her connection

00:15:20.790 --> 00:15:26.112
to the past avatars forever, thousands of
years worth of knowledge snuffed out in an instant.

00:15:26.112 --> 00:15:29.780
Additionally, during this battle, we witness
a world shifting event called the Harmonic

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:30.780
Convergence.

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:34.290
Basically, a portal opens between the spirit
and human worlds, allowing people and spirits

00:15:34.290 --> 00:15:35.639
to pass freely between them.

00:15:35.639 --> 00:15:39.530
At the end of it, Korra decides to keep the
portals to the Spirit World open, a decision

00:15:39.530 --> 00:15:43.960
that reverses the stance of the very first
avatar and fatefully combines the human and

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:44.970
spirit worlds.

00:15:44.970 --> 00:15:47.079
At first glance it seems brilliant, right?

00:15:47.079 --> 00:15:50.839
Wouldn’t the peaceful coexistence between
humans and spirits create a more meaningful

00:15:50.839 --> 00:15:52.110
bond between them?

00:15:52.110 --> 00:15:53.310
Well, not necessarily.

00:15:53.310 --> 00:15:57.630
The unforeseen consequence of these two vastly
different worlds colliding is complicated

00:15:57.630 --> 00:15:59.560
and really doesn't scream balance.

00:15:59.560 --> 00:16:03.750
First, the overlapping geographies of the
world create huge territory issues.

00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:07.950
Houses in Republic City are overrun by vines
and entire city blocks are destabilized.

00:16:07.950 --> 00:16:12.340
It doesn't matter if you're a bender or a
non bender, finding your living room destroyed

00:16:12.340 --> 00:16:17.245
and your building about to collapse, is definitely
on the list of top five worst breakfast time surprises.

00:16:17.245 --> 00:16:21.990
And second, harmonic convergence gives Zaheer,
one of the most dangerous warriors in the

00:16:21.990 --> 00:16:26.290
world, the power of Airbending, which he promptly
uses to start assassinating world leaders

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:28.000
and throw the world out of balance.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:30.690
I'm going to chalk that one up as a big oopsie
there Korra.

00:16:30.690 --> 00:16:34.050
When you stop and look at the totality of
what we know about the Avatars, one thing

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:36.610
becomes clear time and time again.

00:16:36.610 --> 00:16:38.490
This is a vicious cycle.

00:16:38.490 --> 00:16:42.199
Every single one of these avatars dealt with
difficult issues, but their solutions just

00:16:42.199 --> 00:16:45.220
wound up creating more problems for the immediate
successor.

00:16:45.220 --> 00:16:47.149
Szeto focused too much on his own country.

00:16:47.149 --> 00:16:50.149
Yangchen has to deal with and break down isolationist
policies.

00:16:50.149 --> 00:16:54.329
Yangchen helps make peace between the four
nations, but at the cost of angering the spirits,

00:16:54.329 --> 00:16:58.470
Well, Kuruk has to spend his life battling
dark spirits and winds up neglecting the real

00:16:58.470 --> 00:16:59.560
world nations.

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:03.970
Kuruk dies early in battle with spirits, leaving
an unstable political situation.

00:17:03.970 --> 00:17:07.870
Kyoshi creates a secret police to try and
paper over the problems of her country.

00:17:07.870 --> 00:17:11.939
Roku shows favoritism to his home nation,
Aang has to deal with the century long war

00:17:11.939 --> 00:17:14.020
and the death of his entire people.

00:17:14.020 --> 00:17:18.439
All of them ignore non benders, Korra has
to deal with the fallout and the Equalists.

00:17:18.439 --> 00:17:21.410
The Avatar cycle is a cycle of violence.

00:17:21.410 --> 00:17:25.140
It is a broken system and honestly that makes
perfect sense.

00:17:25.140 --> 00:17:29.200
Ask yourself, why does the avatar have to
have a monopoly on balance in this world?

00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:32.540
The very concept of the avatar is imbalanced.

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:36.490
At the end of the day, the avatars possess
the power of a god, literally god of light,

00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:38.480
but they're still only humans.

00:17:38.480 --> 00:17:42.470
Aang was a 12 year old kid faced with solving
a 100 year old war.

00:17:42.470 --> 00:17:43.710
Kyoshi was a poor orphan.

00:17:43.710 --> 00:17:47.200
Eventually, she's going to defend her home
so it wasn't ripped away again.

00:17:47.200 --> 00:17:48.750
Roku was friends with Sozin.

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:52.690
Of course, he's going to be slow to action
and more lenient in his judgment.

00:17:52.690 --> 00:17:56.860
One person holding that much power, that much
influence, it’s a recipe for disaster.

00:17:56.860 --> 00:17:59.273
I feel like I've heard this somewhere before.

00:18:02.380 --> 00:18:06.799
In the end, the really successful avatars
or maybe the least unsuccessful avatars are

00:18:06.799 --> 00:18:08.570
the ones that don't do it alone.

00:18:08.570 --> 00:18:13.210
Aang saves the world from Fire Lord Ozai because
he trusts his friends to help get the job done.

00:18:13.210 --> 00:18:18.407
Sokka, Toph, Suki, Zuko and Katara are all
off playing key parts in stopping the Fire Nation.

00:18:18.407 --> 00:18:21.140
While Aang has his rad Dragon Ball Z fight
against Ozai.

00:18:21.140 --> 00:18:25.950
And those friends are just as essential after
the war in helping him restore balance too.

00:18:25.950 --> 00:18:30.380
His friends helped make and keep the international
peace all in ways that Aang wouldn't be able

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:31.380
to do on his own.

00:18:31.380 --> 00:18:35.370
It just goes to show that controlling all
the elements in this world is meaningless

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:38.600
if you don't also control the element of friendship.

00:18:38.600 --> 00:18:42.960
But hey, if you want more Avatar: The Last
Airbender content right now, go check out

00:18:42.960 --> 00:18:46.409
our previous theory talking about the science
of water bending.

00:18:46.409 --> 00:18:50.050
Yeah, believe it or not but what you see Katara
and Aang doing in the series isn't that far

00:18:50.050 --> 00:18:51.730
out of the realm of possibility.

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:55.710
Or if you want something a little different,
I actually teamed up with Nickelodeon themselves

00:18:55.710 --> 00:19:00.380
and did a video breaking down whether or not
a creature as big as Appa could actually fly.

00:19:00.380 --> 00:19:03.919
It's different, but it was a really fun collab
with the people who made this show happen

00:19:03.919 --> 00:19:04.970
in the first place.

00:19:04.970 --> 00:19:08.210
As always, don't forget to subscribe with
all that new Avatar content.

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:10.730
You know, we're going to have a ton more to
cover here on the channel.

00:19:10.730 --> 00:19:15.790
But until then, my friends remember it's all
just a theory A FILM THEORY!

00:19:15.790 --> 00:19:18.033
aaaaaand cut.

